# ForgeTrail lessons gate (when + how)

This complements **`forgetrail-lessons-mcp.mdc`** and **`forgetrail-phase-status.mdc`**.

## When to run the gate (do it early, before large edits)

Run **`getAntiPatterns`** once and **`searchLessons`** (one or more queries) when **any** of these is true:

- You expect to touch **≥3 files**, or **≥2** top-level areas.
- **New or changed** user-facing flow, export pipeline, or API route behavior.
- The user asks for a **plan**, **feature**, **refactor**, or **milestone** that spans multiple files.
- **Schema / persistence** changes.

**Skip the gate** for: single-file typos; renames with no behavior change; dependency version bumps with no UX/API impact; or when the user explicitly asks to skip.

## How to run it

1. Call **`getAntiPatterns`**. Skim for items that apply.
2. Call **`searchLessons`** with **2–4 short keyword queries** (e.g. `userscript selectors`, `static site install`, `local-only export`).
3. Fold 3–6 bullets into the plan — what you will **do** or **avoid**. Do not paste full MCP dumps.

## Product-facing users

Do not mention MCP, tool names, or “lessons gate” unless they ask how the workflow is wired up.
